  "parsesDescription": "Typed values read back as numbers in the unit's base, per locale; null when the text is no such number. A number takes an optional exponent and, on a prefixed quantity, an optional SI prefix and the unit. Every SI prefix is read, also h, da, d and c that the display never uses; u reads as µ. The prefix is case-sensitive, the unit is not: the unit in its own case reads as the unit, then a prefix before the unit, then the unit in another case, then a prefix alone — except a prefix alone that is also the unit in another case (M for metres, G for grams), which reads as nothing. The locale's decimal mark is read as such; a lone . or , elsewhere too unless it groups three digits (the locale's group mark between a one-to-three digit head and three digits); spaces and apostrophes group by three digits. A logarithmic quantity needs a positive value.",
